* ''No query string overrides the page'' (operator, 2026-11-12: //"I don't like query strings as overrides, that interrupts the tw5 native uri handling (or if we can pipe it through the mirror & tw5 vm it may read pono)."//). A page act never rides a query key: the founding ask moved onto the identity panel's own button, carried across one reload (`?found` left, `aca107a97`). The arrival's relay, floor card and anchor left the address (the relay reads off the page's own origin; the card and the anchor come in at the carriage door). The last keys left the address: the floor reads at the page's own origin (`?flow=` burned), a harness raises the boot trace in the tab's sessionStorage (`lares:c4trace`), and `?mesh=` burned with its door owed in #/the-leaps. A census in `lararium-web` `tests/live-status.test.ts` reads every page source: none reads the query, and the fragment keeps the mirror's permalink and the ceremony document's ask as its named readers.

